minimax-h3-mlx (https://github.com/PipeNetwork/minimax-h3-mlx)

The video VAE tile plan of runtime/video/model/Geometry.cpp, the rotary
tables of install/video/convert_vae.py, the request preparation
(runtime/video/model/Prep.mm: packed layout, rotary tables, scheduler,
timestep embedding, token refiner) and the audio VAE decoder
(runtime/video/ops/AudioDecoder.mm, install/video/convert_audio.py) follow
this MLX port of MiniMax H3, which the VAE converter also imports. Licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).


BigVGAN (https://github.com/NVIDIA/BigVGAN)

MiniMax H3's audio VAE decoder is a BigVGAN generator; its kernels
(runtime/metal/kernels/video/audio_*.metal) implement BigVGAN's
anti-aliased SnakeBeta activations and Kaiser-windowed sinc resampling.
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 NVIDIA CORPORATION.


MLX (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx)

The request preparation's kernels (runtime/metal/kernels/video/prep_prep.metal,
runtime/video/ops/PrepOps.mm, runtime/video/model/Prep.mm) reproduce the
arithmetic of MLX 0.32.1's primitives, so the prepared inputs match MLX's bit
for bit: the fragment order of its NAX GEMM and attention kernels, its wide
GEMV, RMS norm and sigmoid, and the threefry2x32 key sequence and erfinv
polynomial of its random.normal. No MLX code is linked or loaded.

